-- title:
--   The identity series has kernel of degree one
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative ring. The pair `Series.id B` is the identity element of `Series B = Fin 2 → MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) B`, i.e. the pair of coordinate variables $(X_0, X_1)$, so that the ideal generated by the range of `Series.id B` is the ideal $(X_0, X_1)$ of the two-variable power series ring. The assertion is `FormalODModule.HasKernelOfDegree (Series.id B) 1`, which by definition unfolds to three clauses about the kernel algebra $\mathrm{KerAlgebra}\,\varphi = B[[X_0,X_1]] / (\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$ taken at $\varphi = \mathrm{id}$: first, that $B[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0,X_1)$ is a finite $B$-module; second, that it is a projective $B$-module; and third, that for every field $\kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $f : B \to \kappa$, the $\kappa$-vector space $B[[X_0,X_1]]$ pushed forward coefficientwise along $f$ and divided by the ideal generated by the range of the image pair has $\kappa$-dimension exactly $1$. No hypotheses beyond commutativity of $B$ are imposed; in particular $B = 0$ is allowed, no field then receiving $B$.
--
--   This records the degenerate (degree-one) case of the kernel condition attached to a quasi-isogeny of two-dimensional special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules, namely that the identity quasi-isogeny has kernel of degree $p^{0} = 1$. It is the clause needed when the identity acts on Drinfeld's functor, and it is invoked in the treatment of rigidifications of fake elliptic curves and of the Atkin–Lehner and Frobenius actions there.
